/// Chapter 44 of the guide, written from md-docs/reference/built-ins.md by
/// scripts/docsite/guide.py; edit the guide, not this file.
page BuiltInsGuide(path: "/docs/guide/built-ins", title: "Built-ins", description: "Built-in functions, browser values like viewport, query, now and network, string, list and number methods, the built-in types, and browser globals.", layout: DocsShell("Built-ins", chapter: t("nav.group.reference"), blurb: "Every function, browser value, method and global the language gives a program, in one place.", source: "md-docs/reference/built-ins.md", sections: [Anchor(id: "functions", label: "Functions"), Anchor(id: "browser-values", label: "Browser values"), Anchor(id: "string-methods", label: "String methods"), Anchor(id: "list-methods", label: "List methods"), Anchor(id: "number-methods", label: "Number methods"), Anchor(id: "the-built-in-types", label: "The built-in types"), Anchor(id: "browser-globals", label: "Browser globals")], prevTo: "/errors", prevLabel: t("ch.43"), nextTo: "/docs/guide/tokens", nextLabel: t("ch.45"))) {
    Stack(gap: .lg) {
        Markdown("This page lists everything a program can call or read without declaring it: the functions the language adds, the browser values it keeps current, the methods of strings, lists and numbers, the built-in types, and the browser's own globals. [Expressions](/docs/guide/expressions) explains how to use them; this page is for looking one up.\n\nEach function and value has an entry in the same order: what it is, its signature, its parameters and what it returns, where it may be written, and an example. An example of one line is a fragment of a page; the names it reads are assumed to be declared.")

        Heading("Functions", id: "functions").h2

        Markdown("The functions, in alphabetical order:")

        Table(caption: "Functions") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Function").header
                    Table.Cell("Does").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`after(interval) \{ \}`") }
                    Table.Cell("Runs a block once, after a delay")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`ago(date)`") }
                    Table.Cell("The distance from now, in words")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`animate(element, name, duration)`") }
                    Table.Cell("Plays an animation on an element handle")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`beacon(url, data)`") }
                    Table.Cell("Sends a small post that survives the page unloading")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`broadcast(name)`") }
                    Table.Cell("Opens a channel the site's other tabs hear")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`every(interval) \{ \}`") }
                    Table.Cell("Runs a block repeatedly")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`fetch(url, options)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Sends a request through the same engine as `api`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`format(value, .style, option)`") }
                    Table.Cell("A number, date or money as text, in the locale")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`keyIs(event, combination)`") }
                    Table.Cell("Whether a key event is a shortcut")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`keyLabel(combination)`") }
                    Table.Cell("A shortcut as this system writes it")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`log(x, …)`") }
                    Table.Cell("Prints to the console")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`navigate(path)`") }
                    Table.Cell("Moves to a route")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`optimistic(holder, change)`") }
                    Table.Cell("Shows a change now, and takes it back if the action throws")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`replayAnimation(element, name)`") }
                    Table.Cell("Plays an element's animation again")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`rtc(signal: …)`") }
                    Table.Cell("Opens a data channel to another reader's page")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`sanitize(html)`") }
                    Table.Cell("Markup through an allow-list")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`setLocale(locale)`") }
                    Table.Cell("Switches the locale, and the direction with it")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`setTheme(choice)`") }
                    Table.Cell("Switches between light, dark and the system's choice")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`spawn(path)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Starts a script of `public/` in a worker") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`sse(url)`") }
                    Table.Cell("Opens a stream of server-sent events")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`t(\"key\", values)`") }
                    Table.Cell("A translation")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`uuid()`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("A fresh `Uuid`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`ws(url)`") }
                    Table.Cell("Opens a WebSocket")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Every name in this list but `spawn` belongs to the language: a `state`, prop, parameter, loop item or `const` with one of these names is an `E118`. `spawn` means something only after `worker name =`.")

        Heading("after", id: "after").h3

        Markdown("Runs a block once, after a delay, unless its scope leaves first.\n\nSignature: `after(interval) \{ statements \}`")

        Table(caption: "after") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`interval`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Number` (milliseconds) or `Duration`") }
                    Table.Cell("How long to wait")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns nothing. Where: a render block — a page, a component, a branch, a list item. The timer is cancelled when the block that holds it leaves. See [Timers](/docs/guide/state#timers).")

        CodeBlock(#"after(3.seconds) { banner = null }"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("ago", id: "ago").h3

        Markdown("The distance between a date and now, in words, in the reader's locale.\n\nSignature: `ago(date)`, `ago(date, moment)` → `String`")

        Table(caption: "ago") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`date`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Date`, `DateTime` or an ISO 8601 string") }
                    Table.Cell("The moment to describe")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`moment`") }
                    Table.Cell("the same, optional")
                    Table.Cell("What to measure from, in place of now")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns `now` under 45 seconds, then `5 minutes ago`, `yesterday`, `in 2 weeks`, and so on. An unreadable date gives `\"\"`. Where: anywhere. It is the same as `format(date, .relative)`.")

        CodeBlock(#"Text("Posted {ago(post.published)}").muted"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("animate", id: "animate").h3

        Markdown("Plays a named animation on an element you hold a handle on.\n\nSignature: `animate(element, name, duration)` → a handle")

        Table(caption: "animate") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`element`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("a `ref:` handle") }
                    Table.Cell("The element to animate")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`name`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`String`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("A built-in animation (`\"pulse\"`, `\"shake\"`, …) or one an `animation` declares") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`duration`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`String` such as `\"400ms\"`") }
                    Table.Cell("How long it plays")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns a handle with `play()`, `cancel()` and `finished` (a promise). It plays as soon as it is made. Where: handlers and actions. See [Motion](/docs/guide/motion#drive-an-animation-yourself).")

        CodeBlock(#"Card(ref: panel) { on mouseenter { animate(panel, "pulse", "400ms") } }"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("beacon", id: "beacon").h3

        Markdown("Sends a small `POST` that the browser delivers even while the page is unloading.\n\nSignature: `beacon(url, data)` → `Bool`")

        Table(caption: "beacon") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`url`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`String`") }
                    Table.Cell("Where to send it")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`data`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Map` or `String`") }
                    Table.Cell("The body; a map is sent as JSON")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns whether the browser accepted the send. Where: anywhere, usually a handler. See [Send a message as the page unloads](/docs/guide/realtime#send-a-message-as-the-page-unloads).")

        CodeBlock(#"beacon("/analytics", { event: "checkout", value: total })"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("broadcast", id: "broadcast").h3

        Markdown("Opens a channel that every tab and window of the site on this browser hears.\n\nSignature: `channel name = broadcast(channelName) \{ on message(m) \{ … \} \}`")

        Table(caption: "broadcast") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`channelName`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`String`") }
                    Table.Cell("The channel; tabs that open the same name hear each other")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns a channel handle with `.post(value)`, `.messages`, `.last(kind)`, `.state` and `.close()`. Where: only after `channel name =`, in a page, a component or a store. The channel closes when its scope leaves. See [Talk to the site's other tabs](/docs/guide/realtime#talk-to-the-site-s-other-tabs).")

        CodeBlock(#"channel cart = broadcast("cart") { on message(m) { Cart.merge(m) } }"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("every", id: "every").h3

        Markdown("Runs a block repeatedly until its scope leaves.\n\nSignature: `every(interval) \{ statements \}`")

        Table(caption: "every") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`interval`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Number` (milliseconds) or `Duration`") }
                    Table.Cell("The time between runs")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns nothing. Where: a render block. The timer stops when its page, branch or list item leaves. See [Timers](/docs/guide/state#timers).")

        CodeBlock(#"every(1.seconds) { elapsed = elapsed + 1 }"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("fetch", id: "fetch").h3

        Markdown("Sends a request through the same engine an `api` uses: retries, caching and cancelling come with it.\n\nSignature: `fetch(url, options)` → the parsed response body")

        Table(caption: "fetch") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`url`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`String`") }
                    Table.Cell("The address; a value spliced into it is encoded")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`options`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Map`, optional") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`method`, `headers`, `body`; a map given as `body` is sent as JSON") }
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns the parsed JSON body, and throws when the response fails. Where: `await fetch(…)` in an action or a handler, or `resource name = fetch(…)`, which adds `on:` and the other options of a resource. `window.fetch` is the browser's own, untouched. See [Fetch on demand with `await fetch`](/docs/guide/data#fetch-on-demand-with-await-fetch).")

        CodeBlock(#"let rows = await fetch("/api/rows?page={page}", { method: "GET" })"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("format", id: "format").h3

        Markdown("Writes a number, a date or money as text, in the reader's locale.\n\nSignature: `format(value)`, `format(value, .style)`, `format(value, .style, option)`, `format(value, \"pattern\")` → `String`")

        Table(caption: "format") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`value`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Number`, `Money`, `Date`, `DateTime` or an ISO string") }
                    Table.Cell("What to write")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`style`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.number` (default), `.integer`, `.decimal`, `.currency`, `.percent`, `.compact`, `.date`, `.time`, `.datetime`, `.relative`") }
                    Table.Cell("How to write it")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`option`") }
                    Table.Cell("depends on the style")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Places for `.decimal` (2) and `.percent` (0); a currency code for `.currency` (`\"USD\"`); `\"short\"`, `\"medium\"`, `\"long\"` or `\"full\"` for the date styles") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`pattern`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`String`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("A date pattern of `yyyy yy MMMM MMM MM M dd d EEEE EEE HH H hh h mm ss a`") }
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns the text. The locale is the i18n locale when the project has one, and the document's language otherwise; a change of locale redraws it. A `Money` value needs no style. In a string, `\{value:.style(option)\}` is the same call. Where: anywhere. See [`format` and `ago`](/docs/guide/expressions#format-and-ago).")

        CodeBlock(#"Text(format(price, .currency, "EUR"))"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("keyIs", id: "keyis").h3

        Markdown("Whether a key event is a given combination — for a table of shortcuts held as data.\n\nSignature: `keyIs(event, combination)` → `Bool`")

        Table(caption: "keyIs") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`event`") }
                    Table.Cell("a key event")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("The event a `keydown` handler receives") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`combination`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`String`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Modifiers and a key, as `on key(\"…\")` writes them: `\"mod+s\"`, `\"shift+ArrowDown\"`") }
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns `true` when the event is that combination. `mod` is ⌘ on a Mac and Ctrl elsewhere. Where: handlers. See [Keys](/docs/guide/events#keys).")

        CodeBlock(#"Input(bind: draft, label: "Note") { on keydown(e) { if keyIs(e, "mod+s") { save() } } }"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("keyLabel", id: "keylabel").h3

        Markdown("A combination as this system writes it, for a menu or a tooltip.\n\nSignature: `keyLabel(combination)` → `String`")

        Table(caption: "keyLabel") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`combination`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`String`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("As `keyIs` takes it") }
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns `⇧⌘P` on a Mac and `Ctrl+Shift+P` elsewhere for `\"mod+shift+p\"`. Where: anywhere. A `Menu.Item`'s or a `Tooltip`'s `shortcut:` is written this way for you.")

        CodeBlock(#"Text("Search: {keyLabel("mod+k")}").muted"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("log", id: "log").h3

        Markdown("Prints its arguments to the browser's console.\n\nSignature: `log(value, …)`")

        Table(caption: "log") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`value`") }
                    Table.Cell("any")
                    Table.Cell("One or more values to print")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns nothing. Where: actions, handlers, effects and timers. A `Secret` passed to it is a `T12`.")

        CodeBlock(#"log("saved {items.length} items")"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("navigate", id: "navigate").h3

        Markdown("Moves to a route, as a click on a `Link` would.\n\nSignature: `navigate(path)`")

        Table(caption: "navigate") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`path`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`String`") }
                    Table.Cell("A site-relative path; a value spliced into it is encoded")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns nothing. In a single-page build the router draws the new page; in a static build it loads the page's own HTML file. A literal path no page matches is an `R01`, and a scheme a browser would run is refused. Where: actions and handlers. See [Links and navigation](/docs/guide/pages-and-routing#links-and-navigation).")

        CodeBlock(#"Button("Open") { on click { navigate("/orders/{order.id}") } }"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("optimistic", id: "optimistic").h3

        Markdown("Shows a change at once, before the server agrees. If anything later in the action throws, the change is taken back.\n\nSignature: `optimistic(holder, change)`")

        Table(caption: "optimistic") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`holder`") }
                    Table.Cell("a state, or a store's state")
                    Table.Cell("What to change")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`change`") }
                    Table.Cell("a lambda from the old value to the new one")
                    Table.Cell("The change to show")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns a handle with `rollback()`. Where: actions. See [Show a change before the server agrees](/docs/guide/data#show-a-change-before-the-server-agrees).")

        CodeBlock(#"optimistic(Todos.items, items => items.filter(i => i.id != id))"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("replayAnimation", id: "replayanimation").h3

        Markdown("Plays again an animation the element already has, such as its enter animation.\n\nSignature: `replayAnimation(element, name)`")

        Table(caption: "replayAnimation") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`element`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("an element, such as `e.currentTarget`") }
                    Table.Cell("The element to animate")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`name`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`String`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("The animation, such as `\"fadeIn\"`") }
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns nothing. Where: handlers. See [Motion](/docs/guide/motion#drive-an-animation-yourself).")

        CodeBlock(#"Card.outlined.fadeIn { on mouseenter(e) { replayAnimation(e.currentTarget, "fadeIn") } }"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("rtc", id: "rtc").h3

        Markdown("Opens a WebRTC data channel straight to another reader's page.\n\nSignature: `peer name = rtc(signal: send, initiator: Bool, ice: [servers]) \{ on message(m) \{ … \} \}`")

        Table(caption: "rtc") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Option").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`signal`") }
                    Table.Cell("a lambda, required")
                    Table.Cell("How what this side must tell the other reaches it")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`initiator`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Bool`") }
                    Table.Cell("Whether this side makes the offer; one side must")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`ice`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`[Map]`") }
                    Table.Cell("The servers that help readers on different networks connect; none by default")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns a peer handle with `.send(value)`, `.signal(message)` (hand it what the other side sent), `.state`, `.messages` and `.close()`. Where: only after `peer name =`. See [Connect two readers' pages](/docs/guide/realtime#connect-two-readers-pages).")

        CodeBlock(#"peer link = rtc(signal: m => lobby.post(m), initiator: query.host == "1") { on message(m) { heard = m.text } }"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("sanitize", id: "sanitize").h3

        Markdown("Passes markup through an allow-list of elements and attributes, for `Unsafe.Html`.\n\nSignature: `sanitize(html)` → `String`")

        Table(caption: "sanitize") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`html`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`String`") }
                    Table.Cell("Markup from outside the project")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns the markup without scripts, styles, frames, forms, `on*` attributes, or an `href` or `src` a browser would run. It runs at build time and in the browser from the same list. Where: anywhere. See [Show markup you did not write](/docs/guide/security#show-markup-you-did-not-write).")

        CodeBlock(#"Unsafe.Html(sanitize(post.body))"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("setLocale", id: "setlocale").h3

        Markdown("Switches the page to another locale, and its direction with it.\n\nSignature: `setLocale(locale)`")

        Table(caption: "setLocale") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`locale`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`String`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("A locale `i18n.locales` lists, such as `\"ar\"`; `-u-nu-arab` or `-u-nu-latn` names the digits") }
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns nothing. Every `t(…)`, `format` and `ago` redraws, and an RTL locale sets `dir=\"rtl\"`. A literal locale the config does not list is an `I04`. Where: actions, handlers and effects. See [i18n](/docs/guide/i18n#switch-the-locale).")

        CodeBlock(#"Button("العربية") { on click { setLocale("ar") } }"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("setTheme", id: "settheme").h3

        Markdown("Switches between the light theme, the dark one, and whatever the system asks for, and keeps the choice across visits.\n\nSignature: `setTheme(choice)`")

        Table(caption: "setTheme") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`choice`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`String`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`\"light\"`, `\"dark\"` or `\"system\"`") }
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns nothing. The browser value `theme` reads the choice. Any other number of arguments is a `T10`. Where: actions and handlers. See [Dark mode](/docs/guide/styling#dark-mode).")

        CodeBlock(#"Button("Dark") { on click { setTheme("dark") } }"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("spawn", id: "spawn").h3

        Markdown("Starts a script of `public/` in a worker beside the page.\n\nSignature: `worker name = spawn(path, restart: n, timeout: ms, type: .module) \{ on message(m) \{ … \} \}`")

        Table(caption: "spawn") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`path`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`String`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("The script's site-relative address; a missing file is a `D01`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`restart`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Number`") }
                    Table.Cell("How many times a crash starts it again")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`timeout`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Number`") }
                    Table.Cell("How long a request waits, in milliseconds (10 s unset)")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`type`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.module`") }
                    Table.Cell("Starts a module worker")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns a worker handle with `.request(method, params, options)`, `.send(value)`, `.last(kind)`, `.pending`, `.state` and `.restart()`. Where: only after `worker name =`, in a page, a component or a store. See [Run a script in a worker](/docs/guide/realtime#run-a-script-in-a-worker).")

        CodeBlock(#"worker css = spawn("/workers/css.js", restart: 1) { on message(m) { problems = m.items } }"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("sse", id: "sse").h3

        Markdown("Opens a stream of server-sent events, which resumes where it was after a drop.\n\nSignature: `stream name = sse(url, events: [names])`")

        Table(caption: "sse") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`url`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`String`") }
                    Table.Cell("The stream's address")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`events`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`[String]`") }
                    Table.Cell("The named events to listen for")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns a stream handle with `.messages`, `.last(kind)`, `.state`, `.error` and `.close()`. Where: only after `stream name =`. See [Listen to server-sent events](/docs/guide/realtime#listen-to-server-sent-events).")

        CodeBlock(#"stream ticks = sse("/events", events: ["price", "status"])"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("t", id: "t").h3

        Markdown("A translation of a key, in the reader's locale.\n\nSignature: `t(key)`, `t(key, values)` → `String`")

        Table(caption: "t") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`key`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`String`") }
                    Table.Cell("A key of the translation files")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`values`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Map`, optional") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Values for the message's `\{placeholders\}`; `count` picks a plural form") }
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns the message. A literal key no locale has is an `I01`; a value the message does not use, or a placeholder the call does not pass, is an `I02`. Where: anywhere. See [`t(\"key\")`](/docs/guide/i18n#translate-text-with-t).")

        CodeBlock(#"Text(t("cart.items", { count: Cart.count }))"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("uuid", id: "uuid").h3

        Markdown("A fresh random identifier.\n\nSignature: `uuid()` → `Uuid`\n\nIt takes no parameters. Where: anywhere, usually an action that makes a record.")

        CodeBlock(#"items = items.concat([Todo(id: uuid(), title: draft)])"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("ws", id: "ws").h3

        Markdown("Opens a WebSocket, which reconnects with backoff and keeps itself alive.\n\nSignature: `socket name = ws(url, protocols: [names], heartbeat: duration) \{ send T  receive T  on message(m) \{ … \} \}`")

        Table(caption: "ws") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Parameter").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`url`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`String`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("A `ws:` or `wss:` address") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`protocols`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`[String]`") }
                    Table.Cell("The subprotocols to offer")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`heartbeat`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Duration`") }
                    Table.Cell("How often to ping a quiet line")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("Returns a socket handle with `.send(value)`, `.messages`, `.last(kind)`, `.state`, `.error`, `.closure` and `.close()`. Where: only after `socket name =`. See [Open a socket](/docs/guide/realtime#open-a-socket).")

        CodeBlock(#"socket chat = ws("wss://example.com/chat", heartbeat: 20.seconds) { on message(m) { Feed.add(m) } }"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("Browser values", id: "browser-values").h2

        Markdown("The language keeps these values current and lets every page, component and store read them. Each is a name the language owns: declaring a `state`, prop or parameter with one of these names is an `E118`.")

        Table(caption: "Browser values") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Value").header
                    Table.Cell("Holds").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`viewport`") }
                    Table.Cell("The window's size and breakpoints")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`query`") }
                    Table.Cell("The address's query string")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`hash`") }
                    Table.Cell("The address's fragment")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`theme`") }
                    Table.Cell("The reader's light or dark choice")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`now`") }
                    Table.Cell("The current moment")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`network`") }
                    Table.Cell("The connection's state")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`update`") }
                    Table.Cell("A new version of an offline site")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`locale`, `dir`") }
                    Table.Cell("The reader's language and its direction")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`params`") }
                    Table.Cell("The route's parameters")
                }
            }
        }

        Heading("viewport", id: "viewport").h3

        Markdown("The window's size, and which breakpoints it is past.")

        Table(caption: "viewport") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Field").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.width`, `.height`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Number`") }
                    Table.Cell("The size in CSS pixels")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.sm`, `.md`, `.lg`, `.xl`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Bool`") }
                    Table.Cell("Whether the width is at least that breakpoint's token")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("It follows `matchMedia`, so a breakpoint field changes once when its answer changes, not on every pixel of a resize.")

        CodeBlock(#"if viewport.md { Sidebar { Sidebar.Item(to: "/", icon: "home") { Text("Home") } } }"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("query", id: "query").h3

        Markdown("The address's query string, as a map from each key to its value.\n\nA key the address lacks reads as `null`, so `query.tab ?? \"all\"` gives a default.")

        CodeBlock(#"Text("Showing {query.tab ?? "all"}")"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("hash", id: "hash").h3

        Markdown("The address's fragment, without the `#`. It is `\"\"` when there is none.")

        CodeBlock(#"if hash == "pricing" { Text("You followed a link to pricing.") }"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("theme", id: "theme").h3

        Markdown("The reader's choice: `\"light\"`, `\"dark\"` or `\"system\"`. `setTheme` changes it.")

        CodeBlock(#"Button("Light", outlined: theme != "light") { on click { setTheme("light") } }"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("now", id: "now").h3

        Markdown("The current moment, as a `DateTime` that keeps itself current — every minute by default.\n\nSignature: `now`, `now(every: interval)` → `DateTime`\n\nRead it where it is shown or in a `derived` value. A `state` takes it once, so `state opened = now` keeps the moment the page opened (`X06`). See [`now`](/docs/guide/types#now).")

        CodeBlock(#"Text("It is {now(every: 1.seconds).time()}")"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("network", id: "network").h3

        Markdown("The state of the reader's connection.")

        Table(caption: "network") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Field").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.online`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Bool`") }
                    Table.Cell("Whether the browser has a connection")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.effectiveType`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`String`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`\"4g\"`, `\"3g\"`, and so on") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.saveData`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Bool`") }
                    Table.Cell("Whether the reader asked to save data")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.downlink`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Number`") }
                    Table.Cell("The estimated bandwidth, in megabits a second")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.queued`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Number`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("Writes waiting for the connection, with `offline.sync`") }
                }
            }
        }

        CodeBlock(#"if !network.online { Alert("You are offline — changes are queued.").warning }"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("update", id: "update").h3

        Markdown("A new version of a site that has `offline` in its config.")

        Table(caption: "update") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Field").header
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Meaning").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.available`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Bool`") }
                    Table.Cell("Whether a new version has installed and is waiting")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.apply()`") }
                    Table.Cell("—")
                    Table.Cell("Takes the new version and reloads the page once")
                }
            }
        }

        CodeBlock(#"if update.available { Button("Reload for the new version") { on click { update.apply() } } }"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("locale and dir", id: "locale-and-dir").h3

        Markdown("The reader's current locale (`\"en\"`, `\"ar\"`) and its direction (`\"ltr\"` or `\"rtl\"`). Both follow `setLocale`.")

        CodeBlock(#"Text("Reading in {locale}, {dir}")"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("params", id: "params").h3

        Markdown("The current route's parameters, by name. A page also receives each one as a typed parameter of its own, which is usually the better way to read it.")

        CodeBlock(#"Text("Order {params.id}")"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("String methods", id: "string-methods").h2

        Markdown("A string has the browser's methods and five of WebFluent's own. A method it has neither of is a `T16`, with the nearest one it has.\n\nWebFluent's own:")

        Table(caption: "String methods") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Method").header
                    Table.Cell("Returns").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`capitalize()`") }
                    Table.Cell("The text with its first letter in upper case")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`truncate(n)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("The first `n` characters, followed by `…` when the text was longer") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`dedent()`") }
                    Table.Cell("The text without the indentation its lines share, and without blank first and last lines")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`lines()`") }
                    Table.Cell("A list of its lines, however they end")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`words()`") }
                    Table.Cell("A list of its words, split on runs of whitespace")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("The browser's: `length`, `trim()`, `trimStart()`, `trimEnd()`, `toLowerCase()`, `toUpperCase()`, `toLocaleLowerCase()`, `toLocaleUpperCase()`, `includes(s)`, `startsWith(s)`, `endsWith(s)`, `indexOf(s)`, `lastIndexOf(s)`, `search(re)`, `slice(a, b)`, `substring(a, b)`, `substr(a, n)`, `charAt(i)`, `charCodeAt(i)`, `codePointAt(i)`, `at(i)`, `replace(a, b)`, `replaceAll(a, b)`, `split(sep)`, `match(re)`, `matchAll(re)`, `concat(s)`, `padStart(n, c)`, `padEnd(n, c)`, `repeat(n)`, `normalize()`, `localeCompare(other)`, `isWellFormed()`, `toWellFormed()`, `toString()`, `valueOf()`.\n\n`contains(s)` is accepted for `includes(s)`, and `toUpper()` and `toLower()` for `toUpperCase()` and `toLowerCase()`.")

        CodeBlock("derived preview = post.body.dedent().lines().first() ?? \"\"", title: "wf")

        Heading("List methods", id: "list-methods").h2

        Markdown("A list has the browser's array methods and seven of WebFluent's own.\n\nWebFluent's own:")

        Table(caption: "List methods") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Method").header
                    Table.Cell("Returns").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`sortBy(f)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("A sorted copy, ordered by what `f` returns for each item") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`groupBy(f)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("A map from what `f` returns, as a string, to the items that returned it") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`unique()`") }
                    Table.Cell("A copy without repeats; records are compared by their contents")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`take(n)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("The first `n` items") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`first()`, `last()`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("The first or last item, or `null` when the list is empty") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`sum()`") }
                    Table.Cell("The total of a list of numbers")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`remove(i)`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("The list without the item at index `i`; out of range, an unchanged copy") }
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("The browser's: `length`, `map(f)`, `filter(f)`, `find(f)`, `findIndex(f)`, `findLast(f)`, `findLastIndex(f)`, `some(f)`, `every(f)`, `includes(x)`, `indexOf(x)`, `lastIndexOf(x)`, `join(sep)`, `slice(a, b)`, `concat(other)`, `reverse()`, `sort(f)`, `reduce(f, init)`, `reduceRight(f, init)`, `forEach(f)`, `flat()`, `flatMap(f)`, `fill(x)`, `copyWithin(t, a, b)`, `entries()`, `keys()`, `values()`, `at(i)`, `with(i, x)`, `toReversed()`, `toSorted(f)`, `toSpliced(…)`, `toString()`, `toLocaleString()`; and, in an action or a handler, `push(x)`, `pop()`, `shift()`, `unshift(x)` and `splice(i, n)`. `contains(x)` is accepted for `includes(x)`.\n\nHow the methods treat a state:\n\n- `sort` and `reverse` read in an expression work on a copy, so reading a sorted list never changes it.\n- `push(x)`, `remove(i)` and `sort(f)` as a statement give the state a new list, so whatever reads it repaints and a `persist` writes it.")

        CodeBlock(#"derived leaders = players.sortBy(p => -p.score).take(3)"#, title: "wf")

        Markdown("Every one of WebFluent's own helpers also runs at build time, so the pre-rendered page shows its result. A member something declares wins over a helper of its name: a store's own `action first(n)` or `action preview(path)` is the store's, called with its arguments, and a worker's `css.last(kind)` is the worker's.")

        Heading("Number methods", id: "number-methods").h2

        Markdown("`toFixed(n)`, `toPrecision(n)`, `toExponential(n)`, `toLocaleString()`, `toString()`, `valueOf()`.\n\nTo convert, use `Number(\"12\")` and `String(n)`, or `\"\{n\}\"`. To round, use `Math.round`, `Math.floor`, `Math.ceil`, `Math.max` and the rest of `Math`. For text a reader sees, prefer [`format`](#format).")

        CodeBlock(#"derived share = (part / whole * 100).toFixed(1)"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("The built-in types", id: "the-built-in-types").h2

        Markdown("Eleven types come with the language. Each is a plain JSON value at run time.")

        Table(caption: "The built-in types") {
            Table.Head {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell("Type").header
                    Table.Cell("Written").header
                    Table.Cell("Methods and fields").header
                }
            }
            Table.Body {
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Date`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`@2026-03-14`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.year() .month() .day() .weekday()`, `.plus(days: 3)`, `.minus(…)`, `.isBefore(d) .isAfter(d) .isSame(d)`, `.until(d)`, `.startOfDay() .startOfWeek() .startOfMonth() .endOfDay()`, `.native()`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Time`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`@09:30`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.hour() .minute() .second()`, `.plus(minutes: 30)`, the comparisons") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`DateTime`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`@2026-03-14T09:30Z`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("the above, `.date() .time()`, `.inZone(\"Europe/Berlin\")`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Duration`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`90.minutes`, `3.days`, `250.ms`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.days() .hours() .minutes() .seconds() .ms()`, `.plus(d)`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Money`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`€12.99`, `$9.99`, `£4.50`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.plus(m) .minus(m) .times(n) .convert(rate, \"USD\")`, `.amount`, `.currency`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Url`") }
                    Table.Cell("a string")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.host() .path() .query()`, `.with(query: \{ page: 2 \})`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Email`") }
                    Table.Cell("a string")
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.domain()`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Color`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`#0F766E`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.mix(other, 0.2) .lighten(n) .darken(n) .alpha(0.5) .contrast(other)`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Uuid`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`uuid()`") }
                    Table.Cell("a string's")
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`File`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("from `FileUpload`") }
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`.preview()`, `.name`, `.size`, `.type`") }
                }
                Table.Row {
                    Table.Cell { Markdown("`Secret`") }
                    Table.Cell("—")
                    Table.Cell("none: it may not be shown, spliced, logged or persisted")
                }
            }
        }

        Markdown("`.plus` and `.minus` take `years`, `months`, `weeks`, `days`, `hours`, `minutes`, `seconds` and `ms`. A duration is written with `ms`, `seconds`, `minutes`, `hours`, `days` or `weeks`. What the language computes is a call (`due.year()`); what the value already carries is a field (`price.amount`). [Types](/docs/guide/types#the-types-the-language-brings-with-it) has the rest.")

        CodeBlock(#"derived checkout = arrival.plus(days: nights)"#, title: "wf")

        Heading("Browser globals", id: "browser-globals").h2

        Markdown("These names compile to themselves, with no prefix: `window`, `document`, `console`, `navigator`, `location`, `history`, `screen`, `performance`, `crypto`, `globalThis`, `localStorage`, `sessionStorage`, `JSON`, `Math`, `Date`, `Intl`, `Symbol`, `Reflect`, `setTimeout`, `setInterval`, `clearTimeout`, `clearInterval`, `requestAnimationFrame`, `cancelAnimationFrame`, `queueMicrotask`, `structuredClone`, `matchMedia`, `getComputedStyle`, `parseInt`, `parseFloat`, `Array`, `Object`, `String`, `Number`, `Boolean`, `Promise`, `Error`, `Map`, `Set`, `RegExp`, `Infinity`, `NaN`, `undefined`, `encodeURIComponent`, `decodeURIComponent`, `encodeURI`, `decodeURI`, `atob`, `btoa`, `alert`, `confirm`, `prompt`, `URL`, `URLSearchParams`, `FormData`, `Blob`, `File`, `FileReader`, `Event`, `CustomEvent`, `AbortController`, `TextEncoder`, `TextDecoder`, `Notification`.\n\nThe checker types each of them as `Any`. A name the program declares itself wins over a global, and unlike the language's own names, a global may be the name of a state, a prop or a parameter.")

        CodeBlock(#"localStorage.setItem("last-seen", now.date())"#, title: "wf")
    }
}
